D = {
"Eldath|FRHOF": "Goddess of peace, healing, and still waters. Her faithful keep springs, pools, and glades quiet and tend them as places of reflection. They leave broken weapons and reminders of old quarrels as offerings while praying for calm. Many are pacifists or people scarred by violence, and her priests act as mediators who oversee treaties. Striking one of her priests is taboo.",
"Ephara|MOT": "Theros goddess of the polis who sees herself as the founder of civilization. She guards cities and urges them toward scholarship, industry, and art. Her followers pray at midday amid the noise of city life, since honest work is sacred to her. She is most beloved in Meletis.",
"Erathis|EGW": "Exandrian goddess of civilization, invention, and law. Judges and rulers honor her in city temples, and her followers value order, cooperation, and structure over lone effort. She keeps a stormy romance with Melora, eased only when city and wilderness stay in balance. Her holy day, Civilization's Dawn, falls on the autumnal equinox.",
"Erebos|MOT": "Theros god of death and the Underworld, who hoards souls and the treasures the dead carry. He is patient and tyrannical, sure that everything will belong to him in the end. He teaches followers to accept death and misfortune, and those who crave wealth worship him. He seeks to keep the dead in his realm forever.",
"Ezra|VRGR": "A distant god worshiped in several Ravenloft domains, known for dark billowing hair and control over the Mists. Different sects see her as a kind guardian or as a soul-stealing force. Her true nature is a mystery, so the DM and player decide her role together.",
"Flandal Steelskin|MTF": "Gnome god of metalcraft, fire, glass, and alchemy. Legends tell of his huge nose, which can smell the purest ore. He stole the heart of Imix and turned it into an eternal mithral forge, then made Garl's axe Arumdina. Rock gnomes credit him for their talent with devices and alchemical goods.",
"Gaerdal Ironhand|MTF": "Gnome goddess of defense and vigilance. She is grim, humorless, and expert in fortifications, siege tactics, combat, and traps. Her hand was lost in a mishap and replaced with an iron one by Flandal and Nebelun. Gnomes honor her by building hidden, defensible homes with secret doors, spy holes, and alarms.",
"Garl Glittergold|MTF": "Gnome god of jokes, tricks, and clever thinking. He teaches that a good laugh beats a grim mood, that many hands make light work, and that wits beat brawn. He prefers illusion and trickery to combat. He rarely shows himself, usually to settle a dispute that threatens a community.",
"Ghaunadaur|MTF": "An unknowable Underdark entity called That Which Lurks, shown as a many-tentacled ooze or a purple eye. It is random and may reward or torment a worshiper on a whim. Desperate drow with no status turn to it, and even oozes seem to revere it. Lolth's faithful oppose its cults and drive them into hiding.",
"Gilean|DSOTDQ": "Krynn god of knowledge and nominal leader of the neutral gods. He embodies balance by standing back to observe and record events. He keeps the Tobril, a book holding the gods' knowledge, part of which only he may read.",
"Gond|FRHOF": "Faerun god of invention and craft, favored by smiths, engineers, and tinkerers. His temples double as workshops. Priests wander as tinkers and civil engineers, since staying still means stagnating. Whatever they invent, they build two copies, and one is stored in a temple. He grants inventors inspiration through dreams.",
"Gruumsh|EGW": "Evil god of slaughter who drives raiders and marauders to destroy and pillage for joy. He is shown as a one-eyed orc, since Corellon took his other eye. His followers prize fury and strength, scorn the weak, and feel a bloodlust toward elves. His commandments are Ruin, Conquer, and Kill.",
"Gruumsh|VGM": "Chief of the orc gods, who drives his children to multiply and take vengeance on elves, humans, and dwarves with endless slaughter. He chooses his worshipers rather than being chosen, and he marks the ones who prove themselves in war with dreams or visions. Some of those touched go mad, while others gain power and lead tribes. The greatest become Eyes of Gruumsh.",
"Gwaeron Windstrom|SCAG": "A mortal raised to godhood by Mielikki, now the patron of rangers in the North. He is the perfect tracker and animal handler and a foe of trolls and orcs. Rangers see him as one of their own who speaks to Mielikki for them. He has no temples. Shrines are marked by his symbol, a paw print with a star, carved on trees or stones as trail markers.",
"Habbakuk|DSOTDQ": "Krynn god called the Fisher King, who oversees animals, the sea, and nature's balance. Sailors, farmers, and hunters revere him. His holy sites bear a blue bird or a phoenix wreathed in blue flames.",
"Hanali Celanil|MTF": "Elven god of beauty and love, shown as a lovely woman or sometimes a man. Tales of her romances end with hearts sorted out, and elf bards love to sing them. Her priests perform elven weddings and family ceremonies, and few other rites. Her shrines are built around natural pools. She bathes in the hidden pool Evergold in Arvandor.",
"Heliod|MOT": "Theros sun god, proud, sociable, and radiant. He ensures the sun rises each day and values faithful oaths. Court testimony and marriage vows are sworn in his name, and he cannot bear oath breaking. His friendship is warm but can turn to enmity after one perceived betrayal. Nearly everyone on Theros gives him at least lip service.",
"Helm|FRHOF": "Faerun god of vigilance and protection, the ultimate guardian. Bodyguards, city watchers, and vault guards favor him. He is honorable, keeps his word to a fault, and cares nothing for good or evil. His priests teach patience, clear thought, and careful planning over rash action. His faithful are alert and true to their word, though often seen as rigid and merciless.",
"Hiddukel|DSOTDQ": "Krynn god of greed and treachery who rules ill-gotten wealth. Criminals and shady traders worship him in secret. Though he takes their devotion, what he truly wants is their souls.",
"Hoar|SCAG": "God of revenge and retribution, called Assuran along the Inner Sea. People rarely worship him daily but invoke his name when they want vengeance. Three thunder rolls signal vengeance done, and many societies ring a bell three times at a judgment. Prayers for revenge are etched in lead or hidden in diaries, since lasting prayers work best. Bounty hunters and avengers revere him.",
"Ilmater|FRHOF": "Faerun god of suffering, martyrdom, and perseverance who takes on the burdens of others. He comforts the oppressed and the unjustly treated. His priests wear hair shirts, take in the sick, starving, and hurt, and give away most of what temples receive. They put others first and use force to end torture. Martyrs gain rest and reward in his afterlife.",
"Ilneval|VGM": "Loyal right hand of Gruumsh and the orc god of war plans and strategy. Orcs with an early gift for tactics are seen as chosen by him and become blades of Ilneval. These battle captains lead warriors into the fight and strike the moment an enemy is weak.",
"Ioun|EGW": "Exandrian goddess of knowledge, seers, sages, and teachers. She was wounded by the Chained Oblivion in the Calamity, so her worship went underground and has no public holy day. Her followers share knowledge and lore anonymously and teach reason and perception. The monasteries of the Cobalt Soul revived her faith.",
"Iroas|MOT": "Theros god of honor and victory in war. Soldiers, mercenaries, and athletes pray to him, as do common folk who need courage. He backs those who shed blood honorably, and he despises cowards and oath breakers. He is stoic with a dry wit and often appears as a bull-bodied centaur in armor.",
"Jergal|SCAG": "An ancient death god who grew bored and gave up his power to three mortals. They became Bane (strife), Myrkul (the dead), and Bhaal (murder). Jergal now serves as an uncaring scribe of the dead and helps Kelemvor bind souls to their afterlives. He is named at funerals, and some write the dead person's name on parchment placed in the mouth.",
"Karametra|MOT": "Theros god of the harvest, maternal and even-tempered. She values community, stability, and nature's balance, and she watches over family, orphans, farming, and home defense. Nearly every human settlement has a shrine to her, and Setessa is the center of her worship.",
"Kelemvor|FRHOF": "Faerun god of death who is just, fair, and comforting. He leads each soul to its proper afterlife and teaches that death is natural and not to be feared. His priests ease the dying, counsel mourners, and lead funerals. His faithful must prevent untimely deaths when they can and wipe out the undead. Elite priests are doomguides.",
"Keptolo|MTF": "Drow god who embodies the ideal male drow. He is handsome, witty, hedonistic, a flatterer, and a subtle assassin who spreads rumors. Ambitious males emulate him, and some rise high, while many fall to excess or to rivals. He serves Lolth in the Demonweb Pits as her consort.",
"Keranos|MOT": "Theros god of storms and wisdom, merciless and impatient. He strikes mortals with inspiration or lightning with equal ease. Tinkerers, inventors, and sailors favor him, as do those with hard problems. He scorns fools, vapidity, and indecision, and he usually speaks through epiphanies and lightning bolts.",
"Kiaransalee|MTF": "Drow god of vengeance and undeath, called the Revenancer. Legend says she died, returned, and brought an army of the dead to take revenge. Her symbol is a hand with silver rings. Most drow honor her for vengeance, which every ambitious drow needs, and care less about undeath.",
"Kiri-Jolith|DSOTDQ": "Krynn god of righteous war. He blesses those who fight for good and scorns those who love slaughter. The Knights of the Sword, a Solamnic order that hunts evil, revere him most.",
"Klothys|MOT": "Theros god of destiny and one of its original deities. She keeps the cosmic order and left the Underworld to repair destiny after Xenagos's rise and defeat. She is calm on the surface but furious at those who tangle fate for petty ends.",
"Kol Korran|ERLW": "Eberron Sovereign of World and Wealth who guards travelers and guides traders. Trickery is the suggested cleric domain. He favors fair negotiation, and those driven only by greed turn to the Keeper of the Dark Six.",
"Kord|EGW": "Exandrian Storm Lord who delights in tests of strength and blesses those who prove themselves in battle. Athletes and warriors worship him, and others pray to calm his storms. He is shown as a muscled warrior wrestling a beast. His holy day, the Day of Challenging, falls on the seventh day of the second month.",
"Kruphix|MOT": "Theros god of mysteries, horizons, and time, who knows everything ever known. He is quiet and aloof, speaks rarely, and appears as a star-filled hooded silhouette. He rules the unseen and unknown and the brink of discovery, and he is tied to navigation. He can speak to all gods at once when the cosmic order is threatened.",
"Labelas Enoreth|MTF": "Elven god of long life and vigor, shown as an aged silver-haired elf. Elves rarely think of him until they undergo Remembrance. He asks little, only a few minutes of thanks daily and a fresh flower at a shrine now and then.",
"Laduguer|MTF": "Duergar god called the Grim One. He was a warrior who freed his people from illithids and pledged an alliance with Asmodeus against Lolth and the demons. He is the dark opposite of Moradin. Duergar have no temples or services for him and honor him by gaining wealth and power by any means.",
"Lathander|FRHOF": "Faerun god of dawn, new beginnings, spring, birth, and renewal. He is optimistic, if sometimes vain and excessive. People pray to him before trips and ventures, and priests officiate births and weddings and seal alliances. His faith is popular with merchants, and his temples are wealthy and showy, sometimes with phoenix-wing parapets.",
"Leira|FRHOF": "Faerun god of illusion, disguise, and deception, favored by rogues, con artists, illusionists, and actors. She is a mysterious recluse more than a trickster, and she rarely contacts her followers. Cyric killed her and took part of her portfolio. Folk twirl a finger behind their backs when lying to ask for her help. Her faithful guard their secrets.",
"Lliira|FRHOF": "Faerun god of joy, contentment, dance, and freedom. She is honored at festivals and worshiped mainly through dance. She shows herself as whirling lights or joyful laughter, and satyrs love her. Dancers and hedonists are her most devoted, and some train as bards of the College of Dance.",
"Lolth|EGW": "Evil Exandrian god of deceit, shadows, and spiders, who weaves schemes and betrayals. She lost influence in Wildemount when drow turned to the Luxon during the Calamity, and now seeks vengeance. She rules the Demonweb and holds a grudge against Kord, who impaled her with a thunderspear.",
"Lolth|FRHOF": "Faerun god of spiders and the self-styled god of the drow. She is cruel and urges followers to backstab one another. She was once Araushnee, who tried to overthrow Corellon and was cast into the Abyss. Spiders are her omens and Yochlol her messengers. Followers wear web patterns and make blood sacrifices, preferring unwilling victims.",
"Lolth|MTF": "Demanding drow goddess who requires sacrifices of treasure and blood in dark temples. Her favor shows as raid successes, rival houses falling ill, and fortunate births. She is not all-knowing, and some drow live outside her worship. Renegade groups often raise another Dark Seldarine god as patron instead.",
"Loviatar|FRHOF": "Faerun god of agony, cruel and domineering. Pain is an end in itself to her, which endears her to Bane. Her followers hold all pain holy, whether inflicted or endured, and see it as a path to power. They consider a cold, cruel manner ideal.",
"Lunitari|DSOTDQ": "Krynn god of neutral magic and illusions and patron of the Order of the Red Robes. With Solinari and Nuitari she watches over Krynn through the red moon. In myth she is a trickster who fools gods and heroes with illusions.",
}
